{"body":{"asks":"The author's concern of 2026-11-11: code files for common practices lock methods that are then used without reasoning; free-handing in the field could encourage more organic growth. Which of the author's tools, append, thread, session and rewrite, are practices to let go for writing free-hand, the practice said in the field and reasoned each time, and which are writers of a form whose mechanics no reasoning changes, as prose into sentences and words. Leaning: one plain means of writing, a change given to the engine to commit at the command line, as ask reads, its governance the only lock; the practices said in the briefs and the moulds.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M75SHC7MZ3000T"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M75SHCMEQZN000","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Practices free-hand in the field, not locked in tools","prev":null}
